    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company has halted its core fish-rearing operations and is winding down production, pivoting solely to monetizing its Ohio Farm Project assets. There is no mention of robust demand or product-line momentum; instead, the narrative centers on a distressed retreat from the market. The filing flags substantial doubt about the company’s ability to continue as a going concern, indicating a business in survival mode with no clear operational engine remaining.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is pursuing a fire-sale strategy focused on asset disposals and emergency capital infusions through dilutive equity and warrant issuances. A reverse stock split authorization was secured to maintain listing compliance, while analysts assign a consensus Sell rating. These actions, paired with the going-concern warning, signal a management team solely engaged in short-term financial triage rather than value creation, with credibility severely eroded.",
